kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[1]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  add_requirement,"context-must-actually-truncate-when-over-budget",Context assembly MUST actually truncate or compress when over token budget (not just set a flag),"When the assembled retrieval context exceeds the token budget the system MUST actually truncate or compress the context to fit the budget (preserving the highest-priority blocks and partially trimming the boundary block) and MUST NOT merely set a compressed boolean flag while passing the full untruncated context through to the LLM. The truncation MUST follow the v1 _truncate_blocks priority order (history then retrieval then recent then system then query) and use gpt-tokenizer token counting. Current retrieve-and-judge.ts computes compressed=true but never acts on it, leaving the context oversized and risking context-window overflow on large notebooks.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[3]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  "context-must-actually-truncate-when-over-budget","over-budget-truncates",the assembled retrieval context token count exceeds the configured max_tokens budget,the system builds the context for LLM generation,"the context passed to the LLM MUST be truncated to fit the budget (preserving highest-priority blocks and partially trimming the boundary block) and the compressed flag MUST be true"
  "context-must-actually-truncate-when-over-budget","under-budget-passthrough",the assembled context is within the budget,the system builds the context,no truncation MUST occur and compressed MUST be false and the context MUST pass through unchanged
  "context-must-actually-truncate-when-over-budget","priority-order-and-token-counting",the context exceeds budget and must shed tokens,selecting which blocks to drop or trim,"the system MUST follow the v1 priority order (history then retrieval then recent then system then query) and MUST use gpt-tokenizer token counts not character counts"
